# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Read at BUILD time from the repo root by both:
#   - apps/desktop/src-tauri/build.rs  (Rust `option_env!` vars, e.g. SENTRY_DSN)
#   - Vite                              (only `VITE_*` vars; see vite.config envDir)
# An exported var in the shell/CI takes precedence over this file.
#
# THE REPO ROOT IS THE ONLY PLACE ENV FILES ARE READ FROM. `vite.config.ts` sets
# `envDir: '../../'`, so a `.env*` file dropped in `apps/desktop/` is silently
# ignored — no warning, the vars simply come back `undefined`. Dev-only vars
# (below) belong in a root `.env.development`, next to this file.

# Sentry crash-reporting DSN. Baked into the binary at compile time.
# Find it in Sentry: Settings > Projects > <project> > Client Keys (DSN).
# Leave empty/absent to keep crash reporting fully inert.
SENTRY_DSN=

# Clerk publishable key. Frontend-only and public by
# nature (it ships in the WebView), exposed to the app via Vite's VITE_ prefix.
# Dashboard: Clerk > API Keys > Publishable key (pk_test_… in the dev instance).
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=


# Carbon Ads. Free-tier ad strip. Both codes present →
# the sandboxed ad iframe embeds the live carbon.js; absent → a self-contained
# stub renders (no network). From BuySellAds/Carbon after acceptance. VITE_
# (public — the serve/placement codes ship in the client, like the ad script).
# VITE_CARBON_SERVE=
# VITE_CARBON_PLACEMENT=

# ── Dev-only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy the two vars below into a root `.env.development` (gitignored). Vite loads
# it on top of `.env` for `pnpm tauri dev` / `vite dev` ONLY — never for
# `vite build` or test runs, so neither can leak into a shipped binary.

# DEV-ONLY paid-feature unlock: run the app at a given plan tier WITHOUT a
# signed license. One of: free | basic | advance | enterprise. `enterprise`
# unlocks everything (NoAd, themes, MultiWindow, Log-Anytime, TeamSeats,
# IssueTracker) — this is what unlocks the Issue panel in dev.
#
#   1. put `VITE_DEV_PLAN=enterprise` in a root `.env.development`
#   2. `pnpm dev`   (a Rust rebuild is required — the value is baked in)
#
# ONE variable drives BOTH layers. Vite reads it for the frontend entitlement
# store (the UI view); `src-tauri/build.rs` bakes the same name from the same
# file for the native feature gates (`require_feature`), so paid IPC actually
# runs instead of the old "button lights up, backend refuses" state. It is NOT a
# licence and grants NO account identity: `account_email` stays empty, so commits
# keep using git's own `user.email`.
#
# Only `basic`+ unlocks paid things — the tier grants exactly what it really
# sells, so `basic` will NOT open advance-only features.
#
# It cannot reach a release build: the code that reads it is compiled out when
# `debug_assertions` is off, and build.rs will not bake it under
# `PROFILE=release`. Startup logs a WARN whenever it is active.
#
# ⚠️ An EMPTY value counts as "set" and shadows a real one in `.env` (Vite's rule,
# mirrored in build.rs). `VITE_DEV_PLAN=` leaves everything LOCKED — comment the
# line out instead. Both the build and the app say so out loud if you hit it.
# VITE_DEV_PLAN=enterprise

# DEV-ONLY mock API: when "true", fakes a signed-in user (auth.signInMock) so the
# account/UI can be developed without a real Clerk backend.
# VITE_MOCK_API=true

# Graph-theme store backend. Absent/anything-but-"false" → MOCK
# store: ownership lives in localStorage and Buy grants instantly (no backend).
# "false" buys through the official licence server; ownership then comes from
# the verified license. Read by Vite (VITE_*).
# VITE_STORE_MOCK=false


# Licence server base URL (Rust `ADGITTER_API_URL`). NOT a VITE_ var — read by
# the Tauri backend.
# ADGITTER_API_URL=https://api.adgitter.app

